my-id "q-5693" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Evaluate $(\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that $(\\frac{15}{2})$ means the same thing as ${}_{15}{C}_{2}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=15$ and $r=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{15}{C}_{2}\\text{ } & =\\frac{15!}{(15-2)!2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15!}{13!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot 14\\cdot \\cancel{13!}}{\\cancel{13!}\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =105.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-5693/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b720d4-59b0-5d86-b856-ff69abfe4152"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5693"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84959/selection/823a8c49e998a5a9ec284b42c9a0b85925a6439884c1be84dfb11cc4794c81c3" :answer/id #uuid "6623e6b9-5baa-5de3-968d-2bc3b2bdb618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "154" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84959/selection/71ec7720d7077a8c88c1c4a9c53a3f81078793450c23aec02efcc43f1fc689b6" :answer/id #uuid "1f8aac0d-53ca-529f-b8a2-7bcaa3be8880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "82" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84959/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "79556fcb-a415-5d6a-8369-796fe8fd9dca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84959/selection/d539ebd65f03b0cbd95834835c34f2d4f29803032810546c02767346e131cb29" :answer/id #uuid "5240f10b-bf21-5a45-b446-71199a852991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "102" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84959/selection/c54daf1acdfbaf0b57f4320d9c70b1a593612d8d2a4629d0aa35e2678cca1d43" :answer/id #uuid "ee182fd6-3bab-51af-8a43-5cb3892d5ee0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "126" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84959/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "addabf11-05a5-5771-b57c-2340e9a3b490" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84959/selection/c54daf1acdfbaf0b57f4320d9c70b1a593612d8d2a4629d0aa35e2678cca1d43" :answer-field/choices ["q-84959/selection/823a8c49e998a5a9ec284b42c9a0b85925a6439884c1be84dfb11cc4794c81c3" "q-84959/selection/71ec7720d7077a8c88c1c4a9c53a3f81078793450c23aec02efcc43f1fc689b6" "q-84959/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" "q-84959/selection/d539ebd65f03b0cbd95834835c34f2d4f29803032810546c02767346e131cb29" "q-84959/selection/c54daf1acdfbaf0b57f4320d9c70b1a593612d8d2a4629d0aa35e2678cca1d43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84959" :question/id #uuid "e9749e3b-540b-5b96-af63-11e9c05dfa1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-84959" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Sara has a box of $9$ colored pencils. In how many ways can Sara pick a set of $4$ different pencils from the box?" :question/worked-solution "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $9$ pencils in the box, so $n=9.$ We want to select $4$ of those pencils, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different potential sets of four pencils is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{9}{C}_{4} & =\\frac{9!}{(9-4)!\\,4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9!}{5!4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6}{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,024}{24} \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84959/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "120f626e-dd00-537a-8948-d8f81850d696"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84959"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/va