n/math-academy-id "q-84961" :question/is-example false :question/problem "In a high school, eight players enter trials for the soccer team. In how many ways can the coach select four players to add to the team?" :question/worked-solution "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $8$ players, so $n=8.$ We want to select $4$ of those players for the team, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different selections of four players is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{8}{C}_{4} & =\\frac{8!}{(8-4)!\\,4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8!}{4!4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{4!\\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\,680}{24} \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84961/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "120f626e-dd00-537a-8948-d8f81850d696"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84961"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122560/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "21df0986-cc9c-5e88-aaaa-552b3ad956ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122560/selection/07e9bc46a40c356826021ebe569407128c0d312bea1fd767b111c727e40d1018" :answer/id #uuid "1fb4d7eb-d7d1-5831-8ffa-48d536458e11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "220" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122560/selection/04a1c81e5b73e002fd02917f348f820a56e048482c87277df2fc50a5175805aa" :answer/id #uuid "a7f507ba-dbe0-5142-b4ff-7f369148875f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60\\,480" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122560/selection/d16b00060cab28cf08fe96894021875e69f5dc4c89b08c90946a6eac91aacd64" :answer/id #uuid "9138c366-eaf8-59d2-ba0f-f74d47ed896d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,728" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122560/selection/ff778f6775302ce8b078ed4b299e814a54c571c5f88ede03fa1c06ca483a615f" :answer/id #uuid "1371c80b-44d8-5dee-af8d-2b6076c63f42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,320" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122560/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c848416-fa4b-5d60-837d-6c17b0c8b178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122560/selection/07e9bc46a40c356826021ebe569407128c0d312bea1fd767b111c727e40d1018" :answer-field/choices ["q-122560/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-122560/selection/07e9bc46a40c356826021ebe569407128c0d312bea1fd767b111c727e40d1018" "q-122560/selection/04a1c81e5b73e002fd02917f348f820a56e048482c87277df2fc50a5175805aa" "q-122560/selection/d16b00060cab28cf08fe96894021875e69f5dc4c89b08c90946a6eac91aacd64" "q-122560/selection/ff778f6775302ce8b078ed4b299e814a54c571c5f88ede03fa1c06ca483a615f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122560" :question/id #uuid "a1efbaef-38db-5b41-a2a3-7010a9c32c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-122560" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Claire has a bag of candies with $12$ assorted flavors. In how many ways can Claire pick $3$ flavors of candies?" :question/worked-solution "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $12$ flavors, so $n=12.$ We want to select $3$ of those flavors, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{12}{C}_{3} & =\\frac{12!}{(12-3)!\\,3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{9!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10\\cdot \\cancel{9!}}{\\cancel{9!}3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10}{3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\,320}{6} \\\\  & =220.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122560/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d22726fc-8e6b-5e22-80c8-fbc2aa245217"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122560"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122566/selection/72f06d46d987af91ded5a02d558094af020d873ac3a6eade88a59ca51101e80f" :answer/id #uuid "e8a318bf-d8f3-5090-a136-c3673db7ff97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75\\,287\\,520" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122566/selection/6e944ebb6e8fd7e70a327cded0f486a21ce11b05e1cc031eb847063b39266543" :answer/id #uuid "ba31d0ec-cffb-5a55-9d7a-df3a6c23f6bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{100}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122566/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" :answer/id #uuid "c8320cd8-1189-519f-bdae-4fad34e05f6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122566/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" :answer/id #uuid "9e0ea386-5e0f-59dc-8d67-e8a59be407e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122566/selection/9edef25be2423e9bd95da21e2515075a4372c219edef8ec526755994a7ca882a" :answer/id #uuid "5703ad61-c051-505c-b4ad-8a7117a98363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,034\\,502\\,400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122566/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d23bb508-6c11-5d10-a042-339fc62e53fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122566/selection/72f06d46d987af91ded5a02d558094af020d873ac3a6eade88a59ca51101e80f" :answer-field/choices ["q-122566/selection/72f06d46d987af91ded5a02d558094af020d873ac3a6eade88a59ca51101e80f" "q-122566/selection/6e944ebb6e8fd7e70a327cded0f486a21ce11b05e1cc031eb847063b39266543" "q-122566/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" "q-122566/selection/f07223adf063c43bfac440bfcfa1f5e709d54202b4c2c93d5f069881800b6a64" "q-122566/selection/9edef25be2423e9bd95da21e2515075a4372c219edef8ec526755994a7ca882a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122566" :question/id #uuid "f2c342ac-2557-5d89-81e6-2e3e4896aa52" :question/math-academy-id "q-122566" :question/is-example false :question/problem "While Tom was in an elevator within a 100-floor building, it stopped on $5$ different floors. If the order of the floors where the elevator stopped is unimportant, in how many different ways could the elevator stop?" :question/worked-solution "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $100$ floors, so $n=100.$ We want to select $5$ of those floors for the elevator to stop, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{100}{C}_{5} & =\\frac{100!}{(100-5)!\\,5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100!}{95!5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100\\cdot 99\\cdot 98\\cdot 97\\cdot 96\\cdot \\cancel{95!}}{\\cancel{95!}5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100\\cdot 99\\cdot 98\\cdot 97\\cdot 96}{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\,034\\,502\\,400}{120} \\\\  & =75\\,287\\,520.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122566/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d22726fc-8e6b-5e22-80c8-fbc2aa245217"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
